---------- 8. PLL Usage Summary (begin) ----------

+---------------+----------+--------------+----------------+-----------------+---------------+----------------+------------------+---------+---------+
| Instance Name | Resource | Clock Region | Ref Clock Mode | Reference Clock | Feedback Mode | Feedback Clock |     Clkout0      | Clkout1 | Clkout2 |
+---------------+----------+--------------+----------------+-----------------+---------------+----------------+------------------+---------+---------+
|     syspll    | PLL_BL0  |      B       |      core      |      sysclk     |    internal   |                | syspll_CLKOUT100 |         |         |
+---------------+----------+--------------+----------------+-----------------+---------------+----------------+------------------+---------+---------+

Instance Name                 : syspll
Resource                      : PLL_BL0
Locked Pin Name               : syspll_LOCKED
Reference Clock Mode          : core
Reference Clock               : sysclk
Feedback Mode                 : internal

Reference Clock Frequency     : 50.00 MHz
Reference Clock Period        : 20.00 ns
Multiplier (M)                : 32
Pre-Divider (N)               : 1
VCO Frequency                 : 1600.00 MHz
Post-Divider (O)              : 8
PLL Frequency                 : 200.00 MHz

Output Clock 0
Clock Pin Name                : syspll_CLKOUT100
Output Divider                : 2
Output Phase Shift            : 0
Output Frequency              : 100.00 MHz
Output Period                 : 10.00 ns

Frequency calculations:
	VCO = REFCLK * (M/N)
	    = 50.00 MHz * (32/1)
	    = 1600.00 MHz
	PLL = VCO / O
	    = 1600.00 MHz / 8
	    = 200.00 MHz

	CLKOUT0 = PLL / CLKOUT0_DIV
	        = 200.00 MHz / 2
	        = 100.00 MHz

SDC Constraints:
	create_clock -period 10.00 syspll_CLKOUT100

